  "body": {
    "id": "prop:covariance-learnability",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "If \\(X\\) has fixed finite support with every support mass bounded below, the foldwise cell-frequency estimator of the corrected shared-cell covariance \\(\\Gamma_P(X)=\\operatorname{Cov}_P\\{\\Psi_P(O)\\mid X\\}\\) satisfies\n\\[\n\\max_\\ell\\|\\widehat\\Gamma^{-\\ell}-\\Gamma\\|_{P_X,4,\\mathrm{op}}\n=O_P(n^{-1/2}+r_{p,n}+r_{m,n}).\n\\]\nAll conditional expectations used in a correctly specified one-step construction are estimated by the corresponding cell averages.  If, in addition, contrast rank is fixed and its positive spectrum is separated, parametric first stages and \\(\\tau_n=n^{-a}\\) with \\(0<a<1/4\\) give consistent rank recovery, \\(r_{\\Gamma,n}=O(n^{-1/2})\\), and \\(r_{b,n}=O(n^{-1/2+a})\\), with \\(r_{b,n}^2+r_{\\Gamma,n}^2=o(n^{-1/2})\\).  The continuous-covariate \\(L_4(P_X)\\) rate in the original statement does not follow from only a conditional fourth moment for outcomes.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "X",
      "P",
      "Gamma",
      "Gammahat",
      "rGamma",
      "rp",
      "rm",
      "taun",
      "rb",
      "H",
      "n",
      "folds"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:pairwise-score",
      "ass:cell-overlap",
      "ass:conditional-fourth-envelope",
      "ass:crossfit-independence",
      "ass:fixed-contrast-rank",
      "ass:contrast-spectral-gap",
      "ass:rank-threshold-vanishing",
      "ass:rank-threshold-separation",
      "lem:loading-perturbation"
    ],
    "justification": "The proposition gives a checkable root-\\(n\\) shared-cell covariance rate for fixed finite covariate support.",
    "gap": "No continuous-covariate \\(L_4(P_X)\\) covariance rate follows without additional smoothness and tail conditions.",
    "consumer": "The finite-support implementation can learn \\(\\Gamma_P(X)\\) for aggregate-loading and comparator diagnostics by cell frequencies.",
    "proof_tex": "There are finitely many support points, folds, score coordinates, and retained cells.  The lower support-mass bound and overlap imply that every relevant training-cell count is of order \\(n\\) in probability.  Every corrected score coordinate is a finite sum of outcome residuals multiplied by propensity ratios bounded in terms of \\(\\varepsilon\\), plus the target-share correction.  Fixed \\(T\\), the conditional fourth-moment envelope, and Jensen's inequality therefore give\n\\[\n\\sup_{x:P_X(x)>0}E_P[\\|\\Psi_P(O)\\|^4\\mid X=x]<\\infty.\n\\tag{L1}\n\\]\nThus every coordinate of \\(\\Psi_P\\Psi_P'\\) has finite conditional variance.  Chebyshev's inequality in each cell and a union bound over the fixed collection show that the oracle conditional first and second moments, and hence the oracle conditional covariance, have error \\(O_P(n^{-1/2})\\) simultaneously over support points and folds.\n\nOn the clipped overlap region, the maps in Definition \\(\\ref{def:pairwise-score}\\) are finite sums and products, and every reciprocal propensity has derivative bounded by a constant depending only on \\(\\varepsilon\\).  Add and subtract the oracle propensity and regression in each coordinate.  The mean-value inequality followed by H\\\"older's inequality gives\n\\[\n\\max_\\ell\\|\\widehat\\Gamma^{-\\ell}-\\Gamma\\|_{P_X,4,\\mathrm{op}}\n\\le O_P(n^{-1/2})+C\\{r_{p,n}+r_{m,n}\\}.\n\\tag{L2}\n\\]\nAll vector and matrix norms are equivalent because both the support and the score dimension are fixed.  This proves the first assertion and the claim about the remaining cell-average conditional moments.\n\nWith parametric cell first stages, (L2) gives \\(r_{\\Gamma,n}=O(n^{-1/2})\\).  If \\(\\tau_n=n^{-a}\\), then\n\\[\nr_{\\Gamma,n}/\\tau_n=O(n^{-1/2+a})\\to0,\n\\qquad r_{b,n}=O(n^{-1/2+a}).\n\\]\nLemma \\(\\ref{lem:loading-perturbation}\\) gives rank recovery, and\n\\[\nr_{b,n}^2+r_{\\Gamma,n}^2=O(n^{-1+2a}+n^{-1})=o(n^{-1/2})\n\\]\nfor \\(0<a<1/4\\).  For continuously distributed \\(X\\), fourth moments provide only conditional second moments for score products and provide neither a smoothness class nor the tail control needed for an \\(L_4(P_X)\\) nonparametric covariance rate.  Hence no such continuous-covariate rate follows.",
